Content-Description: Where the Hebrew writes the Name, what the Greek writes: Genesis, Leningrad against Swete (Alexandrinus); CC BY-SA 4.0 (Open Greek and Latin First1KGreek, lxx-swete)

"KYRIOS":
  title: "Where the Hebrew writes the Name, what the Greek writes"
  witnesses: "Hebrew: Westminster Leningrad Codex (public domain), via Sefaria. Greek: Swete, The Old Testament in Greek, whose Genesis is Codex Alexandrinus; digital text Open Greek and Latin First1KGreek via lxx-swete, CC BY-SA 4.0, so this article is CC BY-SA 4.0"
  scope: "Genesis 1, 2, 3, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 50: the chapters held in both witnesses; verses are paired by number"
  method: "counted by a script: Hebrew words whose consonants are יהוה or אלהים after at most two prefix letters; Greek words that are a case form of κύριος or θεός (κύριος, κυρίου, κυρίῳ, κύριον, κύριε; θεός, θεοῦ, θεῷ, θεόν, θεέ), accents removed"
  totals: "יהוה 40, κύριος 35; אלהים 87, θεός 101"
  agreement: "39 verses have the Name or κύριος; the counts agree in 28 and differ in 11"
  differences:
    - verse: "Genesis 2:5"
      counts: "יהוה 1, κύριος 0; אלהים 1, θεός 1"
      kind: "the Name in Hebrew; God (θεός) without κύριος in Greek"
    - verse: "Genesis 2:7"
      counts: "יהוה 1, κύριος 0; אלהים 1, θεός 1"
      kind: "the Name in Hebrew; God (θεός) without κύριος in Greek"
    - verse: "Genesis 2:9"
      counts: "יהוה 1, κύριος 0; אלהים 1, θεός 1"
      kind: "the Name in Hebrew; God (θεός) without κύριος in Greek"
    - verse: "Genesis 2:19"
      counts: "יהוה 1, κύριος 0; אלהים 1, θεός 1"
      kind: "the Name in Hebrew; God (θεός) without κύριος in Greek"
    - verse: "Genesis 2:21"
      counts: "יהוה 1, κύριος 0; אלהים 1, θεός 1"
      kind: "the Name in Hebrew; God (θεός) without κύριος in Greek"
    - verse: "Genesis 6:6"
      counts: "יהוה 1, κύριος 0; אלהים 0, θεός 1"
      kind: "the Name in Hebrew; God (θεός) without κύριος in Greek"
    - verse: "Genesis 6:7"
      counts: "יהוה 1, κύριος 0; אלהים 0, θεός 1"
      kind: "the Name in Hebrew; God (θεός) without κύριος in Greek"
    - verse: "Genesis 6:12"
      counts: "יהוה 0, κύριος 1; אלהים 1, θεός 1"
      kind: "God (אלהים) alone in Hebrew; Lord God (κύριος ὁ θεός) in Greek"
    - verse: "Genesis 8:15"
      counts: "יהוה 0, κύριος 1; אלהים 1, θεός 1"
      kind: "God (אלהים) alone in Hebrew; Lord God (κύριος ὁ θεός) in Greek"
    - verse: "Genesis 8:20"
      counts: "יהוה 1, κύριος 0; אלהים 0, θεός 1"
      kind: "the Name in Hebrew; God (θεός) without κύριος in Greek"
    - verse: "Genesis 9:12"
      counts: "יהוה 0, κύριος 1; אלהים 1, θεός 1"
      kind: "God (אלהים) alone in Hebrew; Lord God (κύριος ὁ θεός) in Greek"
  creation: "Genesis 1: אלהים 32, θεός 33, and no יהוה or κύριος. Genesis 2:4-3:24: יהוה 20, κύριος 15; in five verses of Genesis 2 the Greek has ὁ θεός alone where the Hebrew has יהוה אלהים"
  result: "the first translation step is not one for one. The Greek has no κύριος in 8 verses where the Hebrew writes the Name, and adds κύριος in 3 where the Hebrew has only אלהים. That the Name is read as Lord is a reading; where the Greek writes κύριος, and where it does not, is literal"
